# ThunderVox — site-local values and switches (template)
# ======================================================
# Copy to local.cfg and fill in for your server. local.cfg is gitignored and is
# pulled into kamailio.cfg by "include_file" — never commit the filled-in copy.
#
# substdef performs a textual replace everywhere in the config, including inside
# strings, so a value can appear both bare (listen/advertise) and inside JSON
# (push body) with the same definition.

# ---- Server address: at least one of the two below must be set. ----

# SIP domain (preferred): the DNS name that resolves to this server. Devices
# register to it and dial through it (sip:102@sip.example.com). When set, the
# core works through it - advertised in Via/Record-Route and treated as "myself".
#!substdef "!TVX_SIP_DOMAIN!sip.example.com!g"

# Server public IP. Advertised instead of the domain when TVX_SIP_DOMAIN is not
# set; otherwise only accepted as "myself" for devices that dial by raw IP.
# Keep it equal to TVX_PUBLIC_IP in deployment/.env (which feeds rtpengine).
#!substdef "!TVX_PUBLIC_IP!203.0.113.10!g"

# Push gateway: HTTP endpoint that delivers APNs/FCM pushes to wake the device.
# Only used when TVX_PUSH_WAIT is defined below.
#!substdef "!TVX_PUSH_URL!http://push.example.com/api/tv-sip/test!g"

# Service token sent as X-SERVICE-TOKEN. MUST equal the token the push gateway
# expects (SERVICE_TV_SIP_TOKEN in the backend environment).
#!substdef "!TVX_PUSH_TOKEN!replace-with-real-token!g"


# ---- Switches: uncomment to enable. Everything below is OFF when absent. ----

# Park INVITEs for offline callees and wake the device by push (tsilo +
# http_client). Without it an offline callee gets "480 Temporarily Unavailable"
# immediately — the right mode while the push gateway is not deployed.
##!define TVX_PUSH_WAIT

# Digest authentication for REGISTER (401) and INVITE (407). Needs users.cfg
# (copy users.cfg.example). Without it the core is OPEN: anyone can register any
# number and place calls — acceptable only for a closed test.
##!define TVX_AUTH

# Request-rate guard per source IP (pike): >32 requests / 2 s -> dropped.
##!define TVX_ANTIFLOOD


# ---- Provisioning layer (core v0.7+, profile "provisioning" in docker-compose.yml) ----
# Authentication and registrations from PostgreSQL instead of the open in-memory mode. Requires TVX_SIP_DOMAIN
# (the digest realm) and the password of the tvx_sip role (TVX_SIP_DB_PASSWORD in .env). Not yet in core 0.6.x.
##!define TVX_PROVISIONING
##!substdef "!TVX_DB_URL!postgres://tvx_sip:replace-with-TVX_SIP_DB_PASSWORD@127.0.0.1:5432/thundervox!g"
